        "original_id": "4f1810ac-e158-5849-a414-a9f61801e764",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Don Gregorio Alvarez, Luis Walter Alvarez\n- Concepts: Alvarezsauroidea, Alvarezsauridae, Alvarezsauria, Cretaceous–Paleogene extinction event, impact event\n- Roles: historian, physicist, inventor, professor\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Physics\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Walter Alvarez was born on June 13, 1911, and died on September 1, 1988.\n- Luis Walter Alvarez was an American experimental physicist, inventor, and professor.\n- Luis Walter Alvarez received the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1968.\n- Luis Walter Alvarez proposed that an impact event caused the Cretaceous–Paleogene extinction event.\n- Alvarezsauroidea is a group of small maniraptoran dinosaurs.\n- Alvarezsauroidea, Alvarezsauridae, and Alvarezsauria were named for the historian Don Gregorio Alvarez, not for the physicist Luis Walter Alvarez.",
